5487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce2bfa1c-5e37-5680-930e-c063dd6092a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-68957" :question/problem "${(\\frac{6}{7})}^{8}\\cdot {7}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the first factor using the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{6}{7})}^{8}\\cdot {7}^{3}=\\frac{{6}^{8}}{{7}^{8}}\\cdot {7}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the fractional part of our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{6}^{8}}{{7}^{8}}\\cdot {7}^{3}={6}^{8}\\cdot \\frac{{7}^{3}}{{7}^{8}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n{6}^{8}\\cdot \\frac{{7}^{3}}{{7}^{8}}={6}^{8}\\cdot {7}^{3-8}={6}^{8}\\cdot {7}^{-5}\n$$"}]}
